---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Research"
  description="Research and engineering work by Erick Platero — LLM inference, Speculative Decoding, and hardware validation at Qualcomm."
>
  <h1 class="page-heading">Research & Work</h1>

  <section class="research-section">
    <h2>Publications</h2>

    <div class="research-card">
      <h3>Greedy Tree Attention — Fast Tree Attention</h3>
      <div class="research-meta">
        <span>February 2025</span>
        <span>San Diego, CA</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        A compute-friendly tree attention implementation for detached Speculative Decoding
        scenarios. The base implementation demonstrated a <strong>16% improvement</strong> over
        greedy Speculative Decoding, enabling more efficient multi-candidate token generation
        without the full cost of traditional tree attention.
      </p>
      <div class="research-links">
        <a href="https://github.com/eplatero97" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="research-section">
    <h2>Engineering</h2>

    <div class="research-card">
      <h3>vLLM QAIC Backend</h3>
      <div class="research-meta">
        <span>Qualcomm · Cloud AI 100</span>
        <span>2022 – Present</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        Developed and deployed the QAIC backend for
        <a href="https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">vLLM</a>,
        enabling large language model inference on Qualcomm Cloud AI 100 hardware at scale.
        Includes integration of vanilla, PLD, and turbo Speculative Decoding techniques,
        transitioning them from prototype to production.
      </p>
      <div class="research-links">
        <a href="https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">vLLM</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="research-card">
      <h3>Valiant — Hardware Validation Framework</h3>
      <div class="research-meta">
        <span>Qualcomm · Cloud AI 100</span>
        <span>2022 – Present</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        Lead engineer of Valiant, Qualcomm's internal post-silicon validation framework.
        Built on Python, Jenkins, and MongoDB, it automates hardware validation and testing
        at scale across the Cloud AI 100 chip family.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="research-card">
      <h3>MLPerf v4.1 Benchmarks</h3>
      <div class="research-meta">
        <span>Qualcomm · Cloud AI 100</span>
        <span>2024</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        Led benchmark gathering for a private MLPerf v4.1 submission, measuring
        inference throughput and latency for large language models on Qualcomm AI hardware.
      </p>
      <div class="research-links">
        <a href="https://mlcommons.org/benchmarks/inference-datacenter/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MLPerf</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="research-card">
      <h3>H-E-B Smart Customer Alert System</h3>
      <div class="research-meta">
        <span>H-E-B · Intern</span>
        <span>2022</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        Prototyped a computer vision algorithm to form the backbone of the Smart Customer
        Alert System — automatically detecting when customers need assistance and alerting
        store partners in real time.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="research-section">
    <h2>Skills</h2>
    <div class="research-card">
      <p><strong>ML Serving & Optimization:</strong> vLLM, PyTorch, ONNX, Speculative Decoding</p>
      <p><strong>Agentic AI:</strong> MCP, crewAI</p>
      <p><strong>HW Validation:</strong> Python, Jenkins, MongoDB</p>
      <p><strong>Observability:</strong> Prometheus, Grafana, Docker</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
